  message: "PREMISE RE-CHECKED 2026-09-24 at dev 2c63301739, through the production path: analyze_scala, then classify_call WITH dst_ref. The premise holds, except for ONE stale line.\n\nSTALE: `Process.apply(c)` now classifies as scala.sys.process.Process.apply. WI-kilap (#1160, after this row was filed) writes the owner into the module slot, so the slot is no longer `external`.\n\nSTILL TRUE:\n- Companion sugar `Process(c)` still arrives as `scala:scala.sys.process.Process:0-0:Process`, with no call_construct, and is unclassified.\n- Fresh sbt survey: 6 `Process(...)` edges, 0 classified. All 6 are genuine launches from files that import scala.sys.process.Process: Resolvers.scala:135 and :313, Fork.scala:203, Pkg.scala:56 (`Process(\"git show ...\").!!`), ShellScriptUtil.scala:174, RemoteSbtCreator.scala:49.\n- method_starved_modules on that survey does NOT report scala.sys.process.Process, so the false-all-clear still holds.\n- gatling and http4s have no scala.sys.process edges.\n\nNEW DETAIL: `!` and `!!` have no catalogue rows, and the analyzer emits no edge for them. So the launch can only be caught at `Process(...)` / `apply`, which is what fix shapes (a) and (b) target.\n\nInstrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_check_09242026/narij_count.py. Its first version passed dst_ref=None, because Edge has no from_dict. The corrected version rebuilds it with ExternalRef.from_dict, and the counts did not change."  # 382c
