  clock: 4  # 400d
  nonce: 400d  # 400d
  message: "DONE in PR #1171. Fix shape (b): the catalogue rows the name the analyzer emits.\n\n- `module: scala.sys.process.Process` gains `functions: [apply, Process]` under both simultaneous boundaries (fs_write, subprocess). This is the constructor-named-row convention swift.yaml uses.\n- `apply` is re-kinded to function, because it is called on the companion object (ADR-0059). Its ledger entry is gone: 30 -> 29.\n- `scala.sys.process.Process.Process` joined HIGH_RISK_PRIMITIVES (the drift guard caught it).\n\nFILED REPRO RE-RUN ON MERGED DEV 9af3f3ca2e (analyze_scala + classify_call with dst_ref):\n  Process(c).!             -> scala.sys.process.Process.Process  (was NONE)\n  Process.apply(c).run()   -> scala.sys.process.Process.apply    (already fixed by WI-kilap)\n  Process(Seq(\"ls\", c)).!! -> scala.sys.process.Process.Process  (was NONE)\n  control File.delete      -> java.io.File.delete\nBoth boundaries are tagged: simultaneous_boundaries_for = {fs_write, subprocess}. sbt now has 177 classified calls (was 164), and none of scala.sys.process is starved.\n\nCOHORT: 11 scala repos, edge SETS diffed across three catalogues (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/narij_09242026/AB.txt).\n- Shipped arm: +22 classifications, 0 lost, 0 changed.\n- Controls (gatling, http4s, cats, zio) and lila: no change.\n- tapir, playframework and pekko stop reporting scala.sys.process.Process as starved.\n- `Process` is deliberately NOT in ambiguous_names. The rule was set before measuring. All 8 bare `external:Process` matches (the wildcard-import spelling) were read in source and are genuine launches.\n\nThe title condition (\"never classified\", sbt 6 of 6) no longer holds.\n\nRESIDUALS, filed:\n- WI-tipoh P2: scala resolves by simple name and ignores the explicit import. An imported Process(...) links to an unrelated project Process (spark 12, scala3 10). Those launches stay unclassified, and the edges are false.\n- WI-gunaj P3: a fully qualified scala.sys.process.Process(c) loses its qualifier (2 edges).\nNOT ASSERTED: that INV-linub's class statement (\"reaches its entry regardless of receiver syntax\") holds for scala. The two residuals are counterexamples."  # 400d
